#
# holt — Solidity for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract Solidity symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `Solidity`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own Solidity parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"Solidity\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### Solidity ###################################################################
--langdef=HoltSolidity
--map-HoltSolidity=+.sol
--kinddef-HoltSolidity=f,function,functions
--kinddef-HoltSolidity=c,class,contracts
--kinddef-HoltSolidity=e,event,events
--kinddef-HoltSolidity=v,variable,state variables
--regex-HoltSolidity=/^[ \t]*(abstract[ \t]+)?(contract|interface|library)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_$][a-zA-Z0-9_$]*)/\3/c/
--regex-HoltSolidity=/^[ \t]*function[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_$][a-zA-Z0-9_$]*)/\1/f/
--regex-HoltSolidity=/^[ \t]*(event|error)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_$][a-zA-Z0-9_$]*)/\2/e/
--regex-HoltSolidity=/^[ \t]*(struct|enum)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_$][a-zA-Z0-9_$]*)/\2/c/
--regex-HoltSolidity=/^[ \t]*(uint[0-9]*|int[0-9]*|address|bool|bytes[0-9]*|string|mapping)[^;=]*[ \t](public|private|internal|constant|immutable)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_$][a-zA-Z0-9_$]*)/\3/v/
